## 6. Phase 0 Validation Gate (May 2027)

> **All four signal categories start from zero as of April 2026. This is a 13-month cold-start sprint. No signal is easy to obtain. Do not assume any warm path.**

**Gate requirement:** ≥ 2 signals from the list below by May 2027.

**Signal Categories and Current Status:**

| Category | Examples | Status (Apr 2026) | Realistic Path |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Academic signals** | ABDC-A acceptance or strong R&R; ABDC-B acceptance | Zero | P2 (JSIS, first feedback 31 Jan 2027); P4 (CLSR, submit Apr 2027) |
| **Institutional signals** | Adjunct offer / Professor of Practice appointment; advisory panel invitation | Zero | Cold outreach begins Q4 2026; target: 1 positive response by May 2027 |
| **Think-tank / policy signals** | Invited commentary at ORF / Takshashila / CeRAI / NASSCOM-DSCI / Vidhi / Esya / IDRBT; policy brief published | Zero | Cold outreach begins Q4 2026; no warm contacts at any target |
| **Public brand signals** | 5,000+ LinkedIn followers; media citation; op-ed in credible outlet | Zero | Organic growth from current 1.7K; requires consistent cadence + quality escalation |

**Decision Criteria (May 2027):**

| Outcome | Criteria | Response |
|---|---|---|
| 🟢 **GO** | ≥2 signals achieved; Army exit proceeds as planned; solo advisory vehicle registers Q3 2027 | Launch Phase 1 with confidence |
| 🟡 **SLOW** | 1 signal achieved; or 2 signals in progress but not confirmed | Proceed with Army exit; delay full advisory launch; extend institutional outreach timeline |
| 🔴 **NO-GO** | 0 signals; or indicators suggest fundamental positioning problem | Army exit still proceeds (hard date); advisory launch deferred; deep strategy review with advisor or trusted peer before Q4 2027 |

> The NO-GO outcome does not halt the PhD defence or the Army exit. It signals that Phase 1 advisory launch needs a redesign, not that the entire transition is at risk.

